- KeepBoth: Keep both. When a CloudSSO user is synchronized to Resource Access Management (RAM) user with the same name already exists, the system adds the `_sso` suffix to the username of the CloudSSO user and attempts to create a RAM user with the suffixed username.
- TakeOver: Take over. When a CloudSSO user is synchronized to Resource Access Management (RAM) user with the same name already exists, the system replaces the existing RAM user with the synchronized CloudSSO user.', example='KeepBoth', position='Query'),
  principalId?: string(name='PrincipalId', description='The ID of the identity for the Resource Access Management (RAM) user synchronization. Valid values:

